# Concept 4 — Lanes (vertical per-domain columns)

Philosophy: dashboard = side-by-side LANES, one per domain (usually one
per concept). Each lane is a fixed vertical recipe: metric -> chart ->
list. Reading is columnar; comparison across lanes is the point.

```
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
| LANE: Deals      | LANE: Vendors    | LANE: Candidates |
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
| METRIC           | METRIC           | METRIC           |
|   128 open       |   57 active      |   23 in pipe     |
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
| BREAKDOWN        | BREAKDOWN        | BREAKDOWN        |
| open   #### 64   | cloud  #### 31   | screen ### 9     |
| nego   ### 38    | infra  ## 14     | tech   #### 11   |
| won    ## 26     | other  # 12      | offer  # 3       |
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
| LIST (top 5)     | LIST (top 5)     | LIST (top 5)     |
| Acme Corp  $40k  | Cloudly    $12k  | A. Larsen  tech  |
| Globex     $25k  | Hetzner    $9k   | M. Berg    offer |
| Hooli      $18k  | Vercel     $7k   | J. Holm    screen|
| Initech    $12k  | Datadog    $6k   | S. Vik     tech  |
| Stark      $10k  | Linear     $3k   | K. Moe     screen|
+------------------+------------------+------------------+
| ATTENTION (org-wide, full width)                       |
|  COLD: Initech, Umbrella   COOLING: Acme, Stark        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
```

Model: lane = { conceptId, widgets[] stacked }; canvas = lanes[] plus
optional full-width footer widgets. conceptId set once per lane,
inherited by widgets inside (the optional-conceptId design anticipated
exactly this).

Best for: cross-concept comparison, weekly review. Risk: cramped under
~4+ lanes; lanes want equal heights that content fights against.
